		{/* ─── THE FIELD ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The one band about a family rather than a part, and the only one whose
		    subject is a set of states. The matrix is static Astro - two hundred
		    cells of accounting with nothing to hydrate - and the rows are one
		    island: `client:visible`, because the family is thirty live controls
		    and a control that mounts off-screen is a control nobody typed in. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Field, id: "field" }}>
			<SpecimenFieldMatrix />

			<SpecimenField client:visible />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix and the rows read one file: Content/Specimen/Field.ts
				states every cell's disposition, every row's state and the one
				line that says when it is right. A state added there appears on
				both - the matrix's figures and the rows' order - with no second
				edit, which is the same rule the parts table above follows.
				{` `}This band is not on /THE SHEET and that is a boundary
				rather than a gap: the sheet indexes the twelve Dynamic parts,
				one cell and one plate each, and this band is the first one
				about a family of primitives - ten components whose subject is
				their states, which a plate holding one part at 1:1 could not
				print.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE OVERLAY ───────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The second family band, and the one whose subject is behaviour rather
		    than shape. The matrix and the dismissal contract are static Astro -
		    two hundred cells and five rules with nothing to hydrate - and the
		    rows are one island: `client:visible`, because the family is a
		    band of live overlays and an overlay that mounts off-screen is an
		    overlay nobody opened. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Overlay, id: "overlay" }}>
			<SpecimenOverlayMatrix />

			<SpecimenOverlay client:visible />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the contract and the rows read one file each:
				Content/Specimen/Overlay.ts states every cell's disposition and
				every row's state, and Component/UI/Overlay.tsx states the five
				dismissals once for the whole family. A condition added to the
				data appears on the matrix's figures and in the rows' order with
				no second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD follows.
				{` `}This band is the second about a family rather than a part,
				and it is here rather than on /THE SHEET for the same boundary:
				the sheet indexes the twelve Dynamic parts, and a band whose
				subject is the two seconds after a click cannot stand on a plate
				holding one part at 1:1.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE DISPLAY ───────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The third family band, and the one whose subject is the reading weight.
		    The matrix, the verdicts and the conditions' figures are static Astro -
		    four hundred cells and two arguments with nothing to hydrate - and the
		    rows are one island: `client:visible`, because the family is forty-four
		    live specimens including a chart that measures its container and a
		    calendar that draws a month. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Display, id: "display" }}>
			<SpecimenDisplayMatrix />

			<SpecimenDisplay client:visible />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the verdicts and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Display.ts states every cell's disposition,
				both verdicts and every row's state. A condition added there
				appears on the matrix's figures, in the conditions' own list and
				in the rows' order with no second edit - the same rule /THE
				FIELD and /THE OVERLAY follow.
				{` `}This band is the third about a family rather than a part,
				and the first about the components the document only ever READS.
				That is why it carries a verdict section the other two do not
				need: Chart and Calendar are not mounted by any page, and a
				component that is neither used nor argued is a file waiting for
				someone.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE RECORD ────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The fourth family band, and the one whose subject is what the
		    document is BELIEVED for. The matrix, the improvements and the
		    observations are static Astro - a hundred and ninety-two cells and
		    fifteen arguments with nothing to hydrate - and so are the rows:
		    this family ships no JavaScript at all, because a ledger is a
		    `<dl>`, a matrix a `<table>`, a rail an `<ol>` and a register a
		    `<p>`. The only interactive thing any of them prints is a ledger
		    row's `<details>`, and the browser owns that. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Record, id: "record" }}>
			<SpecimenRecordMatrix />

			<SpecimenRecord />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Record.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the condition that
				produced it, the three observations this card did not fix, and
				every row's state. A condition added there appears on the
				matrix's figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows'
				order with no second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE
				OVERLAY and /THE DISPLAY follow.
				{` `}This band is the fourth about a family rather than a part,
				and the first whose subject is trust rather than use: a reader
				does not touch a ledger, they check the project against it. That
				is why its improvements section exists where the other three
				families' bands do not need one - a fact that has lost its
				adverse state is a fact that lies, and a lie is the one defect
				this family cannot survive.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE NARRATIVE ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The fifth family band, and the one whose subject is what the document
		    is TOLD: the band that opens a subject, the stage that explains an
		    order, the figure that shows evidence, the well that hands over a
		    command, the transcript that records a session, the failure that
		    explains a dead end. The matrix, the improvements and the
		    observations are static Astro - two hundred and eighty-five cells and
		    twenty-three arguments with nothing to hydrate - and so are the rows:
		    this family ships no JavaScript of its own, because the only
		    interactive things it prints are `<details>` disclosures and the copy
		    control two of its blocks already wire. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Narrative, id: "narrative" }}>
			<SpecimenNarrativeMatrix />

			<SpecimenNarrative />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Narrative.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the condition that
				produced it, the four observations this card did not fix, and
				every row's state. A condition added there appears on the
				matrix's figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows'
				order with no second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE
				OVERLAY, /THE DISPLAY and /THE RECORD follow.
				{` `}This band is the fifth about a family rather than a part,
				and the first whose subject is a SENTENCE: a ledger is checked, a
				display is read, an overlay is dismissed, and a narrative block is
				the thing a reader is told. That is why its improvements section
				carries the three behaviours the brief named by hand - a stage
				that can advance, a well that can wrap long lines, a figure that
				can open - and why each of them is a prop of the block itself
				rather than a wrapper around it.
				{` `}{NarrativeSpecimens.length} rows, {` `}four groups, and not
				one of them is a screenshot: every state is mounted live, because
				a picture of a state cannot be composed with.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE FRAME ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The sixth family band, and the first whose subject is the frame
		    rather than the content: the shell that decides whether a page can
		    be read at all. The matrix, the improvements and the observations
		    are static Astro - four hundred and forty cells and fifteen
		    arguments with nothing to hydrate - and so are the rows: this
		    family ships no JavaScript, because a shell is a grid, a rail a
		    list, a seam a 1px track and a plate a figure. The only
		    interactive things any row prints are `<details>` disclosures and
		    the print button, and the browser owns both. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Frame, id: "frame" }}>
			<SpecimenFrameMatrix />

			<SpecimenFrame />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Frame.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the condition that
				produced it, the four observations this card did not fix, and
				every row's arm. A condition added there appears on the
				matrix's figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows'
				order with no second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE
				OVERLAY, /THE DISPLAY, /THE RECORD and /THE NARRATIVE follow.
				{` `}This band is the sixth about a family rather than a part,
				and the first whose subject is not what the document says but
				what it sits in. That is why its five compositions are columns
				of the matrix and not a paragraph: a page with no rail, a page
				with two, a shell inside a shell, a pane pair at 640px and a
				plate with no image are not states a component can be in - they
				are the frame's own worst combinations, and a frame that
				survives them is a frame whose design is real.
				{` `}{FrameSpecimens.length} rows, seven groups, and not one of
				them is a screenshot: every composition is mounted live,
				because a picture of a shell cannot be re-composed with.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE READING ───────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The seventh family band, and the one whose subject is the reader's
		    PLACE: the rail, the contents, the index card, the article, the
		    appendix, the folio, the see-also and the leader. The matrix, the
		    improvements and the observations are static Astro - three hundred
		    and thirty-six cells and eleven arguments with nothing to hydrate -
		    and so are the rows, except the crate viewer whose tab bar is the
		    family's own script, scoped to its own root because the sheet mounts
		    it three times. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Reading, id: "reading" }}>
			<SpecimenReadingMatrix />

			<SpecimenReading />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Reading.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the condition that
				produced it, the four observations this card did not fix, and
				every row's arm. A condition added there appears on the matrix's
				figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows' order with no
				second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE OVERLAY, /THE
				DISPLAY, /THE RECORD, /THE NARRATIVE and /THE FRAME follow.
				{` `}This band is the seventh about a family rather than a part,
				and the first whose subject is not what the document says, sits in
				or is believed for, but whether a reader can FIND it: a rail that
				says where you are in the manual, a contents list that says where
				you are in the page, a folio that says where you have got to. That
				is why its six named compositions are columns of the matrix and
				not a paragraph - a document with one section, a document with
				ninety, a heading wider than the rail, an article with no summary,
				a foot with no cross-references and a strip at 640px are not states
				a block can be in; they are the furniture's own worst
				combinations, and furniture that survives them is furniture whose
				design is real.
				{` `}{ReadingSpecimens.length} rows, six groups, and not one of them
				is a screenshot: every state is mounted live, because a picture of
				a state cannot be composed with.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE COMPOSITION ───────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The eighth family band, and the first whose subject is the
		    MARKETING layer rather than a surface: the hero, the bands, the
		    cards, the manifest, the marks and the thirty-five `Dynamic/*`
		    adapters that were built to be the schema layer between content
		    and surface. The matrix, the verdicts, the improvements and the
		    observations are static Astro - one thousand three hundred and
		    ninety-two cells and forty-five arguments with nothing to
		    hydrate - and the rows are one island: `client:visible`,
		    because the family mounts the hero, and a hero that hydrates
		    off-screen is a hero nobody scrolled to. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Composition, id: "composition" }}>
			<SpecimenCompositionMatrix />

			<SpecimenComposition />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the verdicts and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Composition.ts states every cell's
				disposition, every part's verdict with the importers the tree
				has at this commit, every behaviour the exploration produced,
				the five observations this card did not fix, and every row's
				arm. A condition added there appears on the matrix's figures,
				in the columns' own list and in the rows' order with no second
				edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE OVERLAY, /THE DISPLAY,
				/THE RECORD, /THE NARRATIVE, /THE FRAME and /THE READING
				follow.
				{` `}This band is the eighth about a family rather than a part,
				and the first that has to argue a LAYER rather than a block:
				of the {Verdicts.length} `Dynamic/*` parts, {LabCount} are
				mounted only by this sheet and {OrphanCount} by nothing at
				all. That is why its verdicts section exists where the other
				seven families' bands do not need one - a part with no
				importer is not a design defect, it is a decision the owner
				has not made yet, and this sheet's job is to print the
				evidence for the decision rather than to make it.
				{` `}{CompositionSpecimenCount} rows, eight groups, and not one
				of them is a screenshot: every composition is mounted live,
				because a picture of a hero cannot be re-composed with.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE SMALL SURFACES ────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The ninth family band, and the first whose subject is what the
		    document does when the reader is LOCKED OUT: the credential
		    routes, the account directory, the legal set's clause and its
		    rail, the contact routes and the four reference blocks. The
		    matrix, the improvements and the observations are static Astro -
		    three hundred and eighty-four cells and twenty-three arguments with
		    nothing to hydrate - and so are the rows, except `AuthReport`,
		    which is a React component rendered server-side with no client
		    directive because it has no state, no handler and no hook. The
		    two islands the family owns - the contact form and the auth gate
		    - are mounted by the routes that need them, and the workspace's
		    `form` slot is what lets the plate print the composition without
		    hydrating either. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Small, id: "small" }}>
			<SpecimenSmallMatrix />

			<SpecimenSmall />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Small.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the condition
				that produced it, the five observations this card did not fix,
				and every row's arm. A condition added there appears on the
				matrix's figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows'
				order with no second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE
				OVERLAY, /THE DISPLAY, /THE RECORD, /THE NARRATIVE, /THE
				FRAME, /THE READING and /THE COMPOSITION follow.
				{` `}This band is the ninth about a family rather than a part,
				and the first whose subject is the page a reader reaches when
				they cannot get in. That is why its seven compositions are
				columns of the matrix and not a paragraph - signed out,
				signing in, signed in, expired, denied, a failed submit and a
				missing clause are not states a block can be in; they are the
				states these pages are READ in, and a small surface that
				survives them is a small surface whose design frame is real.
				{` `}{SmallSpecimens.length} rows, six groups, and not one of
				them is a screenshot: every state is mounted live, because a
				picture of a locked-out page cannot be re-composed with.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE APPARATUS ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		{/* The tenth family band, and the last before the stock: the parts that
		    make the document work rather than say something. Motion, the
		    specimen surface's own blocks and this card's gallery index, the
		    head, the runtime providers, the trail and the blog. They are one
		    family because they fail in one way - silently - and the seven
		    compositions the brief named by hand are columns of the matrix
		    rather than prose. The matrix and the two argument sections are
		    static Astro; the rows are static too, except `MotionOrigin`, the
		    family's one island, mounted `client:visible` exactly as `/Motion`
		    mounts it. The providers render no markup, so their rows print the
		    contract each one exposes, and the head's rows print the tags
		    `TagsOf()` returns - the function the head itself renders from. */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Apparatus, id: "apparatus" }}>
			<SpecimenApparatusMatrix />

			<SpecimenApparatus />

			<p class="specimen-page__note">
				The matrix, the improvements and the rows read one file:
				Content/Specimen/Apparatus.ts states every cell's disposition,
				every behaviour the exploration produced with the cell that
				produced it, the five observations this card did not fix, and
				every row's arm. A condition added there appears on the matrix's
				figures, in the columns' own list and in the rows' order with no
				second edit - the same rule /THE FIELD, /THE OVERLAY, /THE
				DISPLAY, /THE RECORD, /THE NARRATIVE, /THE FRAME, /THE READING,
				/THE COMPOSITION and /THE SMALL SURFACES follow.
				{` `}This band is the tenth about a family rather than a part, and
				the first whose subject is what the document does when it is
				working: a motion that explains a change, a specimen that shows
				one, a head that states one, a provider that carries one. That is
				why its seven compositions are columns of the matrix and not a
				paragraph - reduced motion, no trigger, no image, no logo,
				unfurled, offline and unconfigured are not states a block is
				styled for; they are the conditions under which the apparatus
				either tells the truth or lies by omission.
				{` `}{ApparatusSpecimenCount} rows, seven groups, and not one of
				them is a screenshot: every state is mounted live, and the three
				that cannot be mounted - the head, the two providers and the
				pageview walker - print the contract they expose rather than a
				picture of a context.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE MATERIAL ──────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Material, id: "material" }}>
			<SpecimenMaterial
				items={Material}
				label="MATERIAL"
				count={`${Material.length} SPECIMENS`}
				empty="No specimen is filed, so the strip prints nothing. The material is not a preference that can be missing: it is read from the token sheet, and a strip with no rows is a build that lost the file."
			/>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE REGISTER ──────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Register, id: "register" }}>
			<div class="specimen-page__register">
				<RecordLedger
